Context: Grothendieck is building a theory of 'déploiement' (unfolding) of stratified spaces. Its basic tools are cylindrical neighbourhoods (collars) E_B ≃ B × I, I = [0,1], of 'bordant' parts B, each with homotheties λ_E for λ in ]0,1]. Alongside these he uses conical neighbourhoods T of a closed subspace Y ⊂ X, with a 'partie-bord' Ṫ and a projection Ṫ → Y.

(1) Lines 1–2 end the proposition from the previous page. The data are germs of cylindrical structures compatible with a conical structure described by (X̃, Ẋ, p: Ẋ → Y). Condition b) requires Ẋ_0 = p^{-1}(Y_0) and collars Ẋ_0 × I, Y_0 × I in the given germs. With these collars, p restricted to Ẋ_0 × I maps into Y_0 × I and is identified with p_0 × id_I, where p_0 : Ẋ_0 → Y_0. In other words, p is a collared map, a morphism of collared pairs.

(2) Definition of transversality (the word 'Transversalité' replaces a crossed-out 'Compatibilité'). Take a finite family (B_i, E_{B_i}) of cylindrical neighbourhoods of parts B_i of X. For each J ⊂ I set E_J := ∩_{i∈J} E_{B_i} and B_J := ∩_{i∈J} B_i. The family is transversal if:
- E_J ≃ B_J × I^J;
- for each j ∈ J, the homothety λ of E_{B_j} induces on E_J the map (b, (t_α)) ↦ (b, (t'_α)), with t'_α = t_α for α ≠ j and t'_α = λ t_α for α = j;
- equivalently, E_J is cylindrical inside each E_{B_j}, compatibly.
This is exactly a system of commuting, mutually compatible collars along codimension-|J| corners. Locally X looks like B_J × [0,1]^J, the corner model of a manifold with corners / ⟨n⟩-manifold.

(3) Transversality of such a family with a conical neighbourhood T of Y ⊂ X. For every J, inside E_J ≃ B_J × I^J one requires:
- E_J ∩ T ≃ T_J × I^J, with T_J = T ∩ B_J;
- this induces Ė_J ∩ Ṫ ≃ Ṫ_J × I^J;
- and E_J ∩ Y ≃ Y_J × I^J, with Y_J = Y ∩ B_J.
The next page adds that the conical structure on E_J ∩ T is the product, by I^J, of a conical structure on (T_J, Y_J).

Purpose: these are the corner-compatibility conditions needed to assemble, stratum by stratum, the unfolding of a stratified space into a 'manifold with corners' whose faces are indexed by boolean intervals. That is the condition on the poset of strata stated on the following page, where intervals [i, j] are anti-isomorphic to P(S).
